<!-- The E.D. Pa. Bankruptcy motion's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs;
     docs/EVAL-LOOP.md, "Cross-engine gate") in the face of the typst template ({font}, Times New Roman; no E.D. Pa.
     rule names a face, see ../README.md) at 12 pt (size 24 half points); Body Text in exact 24 pt line boxes (480
     twips, typst pitch-body: double spaced) with a half-inch first-line indent (typst para-indent); single lines in
     14 pt boxes (280 twips, typst pitch-single). docx/paeb-motion-brief.lua writes every paragraph itself: the court
     title, the caption (FRBP 9004(b)), the title, the lead-in and consent statement, the memorandum paragraphs, the
     headings, the lists, the signature block, the certificate of service (L.B.R. 9014-4), the footer (the page
     number, centred, its line box ending 0.5 in above the edge: typst footer-descent) and the section (letter, 1 in
     margins; L.B.R. 9004-1(b)). Twips: 20 x pt. pandoc-from: CommonMark with smart punctuation, as typst's cmarker
     reads the body. -->
<reference xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" base="xengine" pandoc-from="commonmark+smart+yaml_metadata_block" size="24" body="480" single="280" indent="720" heading="480" heading-before="240" heading-after="240" footer="720">
</reference>
